# ANSI art frames are escape sequences, not prose. Git detected them as text, so a
# Windows checkout would rewrite every LF to CRLF and the animation would render as
# a shredded screen — on a machine where nobody would think to look, because the
# frames are only ever played on a Linux target.
*.ans -text
*.ans.gz binary

# Shell scripts that run on the installed box. A CRLF shebang line is `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`,
# which fails with the famously unhelpful "bad interpreter: No such file or directory".
*.sh text eol=lf
